# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an [[open relationship]] or [[open marriage|marriage]], i.e., with possible additional relationships.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Jenny Block|chapter=You Can’t Run Out of Love|title=Open: Love, Sex, and Life in an Open Marriage|edition=2nd|location=Berkeley, Calif.|publisher=[[w:Perseus Books Group|Seal Press]]|page=172|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/openlovesexlifei0000bloc/page/172/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-58005-275-7|passage=He assured me, unequivocally, that he was, and that he rather enjoyed the side benefits of my trysts: I was happier and living more honestly, as well as off his back about many of the issues that had been troublesome for me before we '''opened''' our relationship.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Rhea Orion|quotee=Annika|chapter=Case Excerpt: Annika|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=AVNPDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT216|title=A Therapist’s Guide to Consensual Nonmonogamy: Polyamory, Swinging, and Open Marriage|location=New York, N.Y.&#59; Abingdon, Oxfordshire|publisher=w:Routledge|section=part II (Issues and Interventions), chapter 9 (Sex and Consensual Nonmonogamy)|isbn=978-1-315-46225-7|passage=I wouldn’t do it unless there is a reason for it, I wouldn’t '''open''' a marriage just for fun. I think it’s too dangerous. I know I’m a monogamous type of person—I like just one person at a time; actually sleeping with more than one person in separate relationships is too confusing.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023|author=James K. Beggan|chapter=How Do We Make Decisions?|title=The Decisions to '''Open''' a Relationship: To Three or Not to Three|location=Lanham, Md.|publisher=[[w:Rowman & Littlefield|Lexington Books]]|page=90|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=_hTWEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA90|isbn=9781666939958|passage=Social situations involved in '''opening''' relationships are uncertain, rather than risky, environments. Although some people might say, “Absolutely not,” it may be difficult to predict the likelihood people will respond favorably to the prospect, in part because a wide range of unknown or unknowable factors may drive their willingness.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[disclose]]; to [[reveal]]; to [[interpret]]; to [[explain]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1622|author=w:Francis Bacon|title=The History of the Reign of King Henry the Seventh
|passage=The king '''opened''' himself to some of his council, that he was sorry for the earl's death.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Jeremiah|chapter=20|verse=12|passage=Unto thee have I '''opened''' my cause.}}

====Usage notes====
* Due to the near-opposite meanings relating to fluid flow and electrical components, these usages are deprecated in safety-critical instructions, with the words ''to on'' or ''to off'' preferred, so instead of ''Open valve A; open switch B'' use ''Turn valve A to ON; turn switch B to OFF''.

