|passage=he was condemned to die for the felony, and being so well known for an old offender, had certainly died, but the merchant, upon his earnest application, had '''obtained''' that he should be transported, on condition that he restored all the rest of his bills, which he had done accordingly.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To [[prevail]], be [[victorious]]; to [[succeed]]. {{defdate|15th–19th c.}}
